      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Synchronicity, a term coined by Carl Jung, suggests meaningful coincidences that are not causally related, yet feel deeply connected to an internal state. While this idea describes a pattern of meaningful alignment, it remains a philosophical or psychological concept rather than a testable scientific mechanism. If you are consistently noticing these connections, it strongly suggests that your underlying focus and expectations are profoundly shaping what you pay attention to in your daily life.",
